{"message":"Yes—but not with Green Account. Green has no automatic overdraft transfers, so an insufficient-funds transaction is declined.

**Blue Account (checking)** supports the safety net you want: you can link an eligible savings account, and automatic transfers can cover a shortfall. Each protection-triggered transfer costs **$12.50**, while the account itself charges **no overdraft fee**. The transfer fee can apply even if it covers only part of the shortfall. You can change or remove the linked funding source later.

Blue Account also has a $20 monthly maintenance fee, waived with a minimum daily balance of $625. If this works for you, would you like to proceed with opening a **Blue Account** and then linking your savings account for overdraft protection?"}

{"message":"Your Blue Account makes **Silver Plus Account** the strongest confirmed match. Blue Account provides a **+0.35% APY boost** when paired with Silver Plus, and Silver Plus includes savings-goal tracking, automatic debit-card round-ups, and a **0.25% direct-deposit APY bonus** when eligible. I don’t want to quote a base APY without a confirmed current rate for this account.

There is one timing requirement: personal savings accounts require an active checking account held for at least **14 days**. Your Blue Account was opened today, November 14, 2025, so you should become eligible on **November 28, 2025**, provided your accounts remain in good standing. Once opened, you’ll have 30 days to fund the savings account or it may be closed.

The best next step is to open **Silver Plus Account** on or after November 28 and then, if you authorize it, transfer your chosen opening amount from your Blue Account."}

{"message":"A decline can happen even when you have available credit. Common causes include fraud protection flagging an unusual purchase, incorrect card details, a card that has not been activated, an expired card, international-use restrictions, a merchant terminal problem, or a temporary processing issue.

Please check that your card number, expiration date, and CVV are correct; confirm the card is activated and unexpired; retry once; and, if possible, try another terminal or merchant. If declines continue, Rho-Bank can review holds, restrictions, and fraud alerts on the account. You can contact us at 1-800-RHO-BANK, through the mobile app, or at rhobank.com/help.

If you share whether this is happening at one merchant or several, and whether the purchases are domestic or international, I can help narrow down the likely cause."}

{"message":"I can help. One timing note: personal savings eligibility requires holding an active checking account for at least 14 days. Since your Blue Account opened today, the earliest date I can open a savings account is **11/28/2025**.

For growth, my preliminary recommendation is the **Silver Plus Account** because it qualifies for a **+0.35% APY boost** when linked to your Blue Account. If you have at least **$50,000** to keep in savings, the **Platinum Account** may be stronger: it earns **6.5% APY**, but requires maintaining $50,000 and may charge a $25 monthly fee below that threshold.

Which amount is closest to what you plan to deposit: **under $5,000, $5,000–$49,999, or $50,000 and above**?"}

